# PrepWise Environment Configuration
# 
# This is an EXAMPLE file. Copy this to .env.local and fill in your actual values.
# NEVER commit .env.local to git - it contains sensitive credentials!
# 
# For local development: Create .env.local in the root directory
# For production: Set these variables in your deployment platform

# ==========================================
# VAPI AI - Voice Interview Agent
# ==========================================
# Get these from: https://vapi.ai
# 
# Web token for client-side Vapi integration
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPI_WEB_TOKEN=your_vapi_web_token_here

# Workflow ID for interview orchestration
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPI_WORKFLOW_ID=your_vapi_workflow_id_here

# ==========================================
# GOOGLE GENERATIVE AI - Analysis & Feedback
# ==========================================
# Get this from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikeys
# 
# API key for Gemini AI model (for analysis and feedback generation)
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=your_google_ai_api_key_here

# ==========================================
# APPLICATION URLS
# ==========================================
# Base URL for application
# For local: http://localhost:3000
# For production: your_domain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ==========================================
# SOCKET.IO - Real-time Communication
# ==========================================
# Socket server for DSA rooms and real-time features
# Local development: http://localhost:3001
# Production: your_socket_server_url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_IO_URL=https://ai-interview-socket.onrender.com

# ==========================================
# FIREBASE - CLIENT SIDE (Public Variables)
# ==========================================
# Get these from: Firebase Console > Project Settings > Web App Config
# These are PUBLIC - safe to expose in frontend code
#
# Your Firebase API key
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key_here

# Firebase authentication domain
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project.firebaseapp.com

# Firebase project ID
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id_here

# Firebase storage bucket
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your_project.appspot.com

# Firebase messaging sender ID
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_sender_id_here

# Firebase app ID
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_app_id_here

# ==========================================
# FIREBASE - SERVER SIDE (Private Variables)
# ==========================================
# Get these from: Firebase Console > Project Settings > Service Account
# These are PRIVATE - never expose in frontend code
#
# Firebase project ID (server-side)
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id_here

# Firebase service account client email
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@your_project.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Firebase service account private key
# Copy the entire private key including -----BEGIN and -----END lines
# Make sure to escape newlines as \n in single line
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nYour_Private_Key_Content_Here\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# ==========================================
# NOTES FOR DEVELOPERS
# ==========================================
#
# 1. NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables:
#    - These are exposed to the browser
#    - Safe for public API keys only
#    - Include in client-side JavaScript
#    - Visible in source code
#
# 2. Private Variables (without NEXT_PUBLIC_):
#    - Only available on server-side
#    - NEVER exposed to browser
#    - Use in Server Components and API routes
#    - Safe for sensitive credentials
#
# 3. Setting up Firebase:
#    a) Go to Firebase Console (https://console.firebase.google.com)
#    b) Create a new project or select existing
#    c) Go to Project Settings > Web App
#    d) Copy all PUBLIC keys to NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* variables
#    e) Go to Service Accounts > Generate new private key
#    f) Copy PRIVATE_KEY and CLIENT_EMAIL to server variables
#
# 4. Getting Vapi Credentials:
#    a) Sign up at https://vapi.ai
#    b) Create a new workflow
#    c) Get your web token and workflow ID
#    d) Set NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPI_WEB_TOKEN and NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPI_WORKFLOW_ID
#
# 5. Google AI API:
#    a) Go to https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikeys
#    b) Create new API key
#    c) Enable Generative AI API
#    d) Set GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY
#
# ==========================================
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# ==========================================
# 
# Steps to set up:
# 1. Copy this file to .env.local: cp .env.example .env.local
# 2. Fill in all the values with your credentials
# 3. Run the development server: npm run dev
# 4. Never commit .env.local to version control
#
# .gitignore already contains .env.local, so you're safe!
#
# ==========================================
# VERIFICATION
# ==========================================
#
# After setting up, verify with:
# ✅ Check that npm run dev works without errors
# ✅ Check that login page appears
# ✅ Check that you can sign up and sign in
# ✅ Check that Firebase stores user data
# ✅ Check that interviews can be created
#
# If something doesn't work:
# 1. Double-check variable names (typos matter!)
# 2. Verify credentials in Firebase/Vapi/Google consoles
# 3. Check that FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY has newlines escaped as \n
# 4. Check that strings with special chars are quoted
# 5. Look at console errors for more details
#
# ==========================================
